# Git - Staging to production flow (DevOps spine)

Reference: [autogit/gitupdate.md](autogit/gitupdate.md). Session hard rule point 5 states the short spine (`HARD_RULES`); this rule adds kit naming and pointers. Full routines live in `autogit/gitupdate.md`.

Agent Kit treats this flow as **operational memory**: plan -> handoff -> staging -> prod -> memory. Without a structured promote, handoffs go stale.

## Commands

| Command | Slash | Destination | Use |
|---------|-------|-------------|-----|
| `git staging` | `/git-staging` | `origin/staging` | Working branch, commit, MR, merge to staging |
| `git prod` | `/git-prod` | `origin/main` | Promote approved staging to production |

Factory wrap (not consumer L0): `/kit-staging` / `/kit-prod` when present. Consumers use `/git-staging` / `/git-prod`. Legacy pre-prod names (`homologacao`, `develop`) keep the two-step pattern; canonical name is `staging`.

## Critical rule

- **NEVER** commit or push directly to `main` / `origin/main`. Always via `origin/staging`.
- Commits: **`git staging`**. Production: only **`git prod`** after staging approval.
- Never work on `main`. After `git prod`, switch back to `staging`.
- Install `pre-commit` / `pre-push` guards from [git-hooks/](../../git-hooks/) that abort commit/push to `main`/`master`.
- `git log --first-parent --no-merges main` should only list the root commit.
- Prune migrated legacy pre-prod branches locally and on remotes.

## Flow + memory

```
Plan (.cursor/plans/) -> work -> /handoff
  -> git staging -> origin/staging
  -> (approval) -> git prod -> origin/main
  -> memory-loop WRITE if it applies
```

After staging or prod: update `.cursor/HANDOFF.md`. Closed incidents/decisions: write `.cursor/memory/` (memory-loop).

## Conventional Commits

Prefixes: `feat:`, `fix:`, `docs:`, `docs(memory):`, `refactor:`, `chore:`, `chore(kit):`, `test:`, `style:`, `perf:`. Soft kit paths (monitors, `_index` Audits, versioned HANDOFF) ship as `docs(memory):` / `chore(kit):` when not the product theme.

## When the user says

- **`git staging`** / **`git prod`**: run the matching section in [autogit/gitupdate.md](autogit/gitupdate.md) end-to-end (SoT). Do not invent a parallel routine.
  Staging: warn on dirty untracked `plan-monitor-*.md`; stage memory/monitor files add-by-name only; remaining safe kit dirt ships in a `docs(memory):` / `chore(kit):` bucket in the same run.
  Prod: **one confirm, one ship**. Red or unfinished post-prod verification is a STOP. Done means `main` pushed, tag pushed, tag CI green (plus any project release verification). Never steal the confirmation Ask.

## Troubleshooting

- Direct commits to main blocked -> `git staging`.
- No `staging` branch -> `git checkout -b staging` and `git push -u origin staging`.
- Legacy `homologacao` -> same command; migrate to `staging` when possible (gitupdate Naming).
